WEBVTT

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.690
<i>At last, the day has come.</i>

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:11.860
<i>Hase...</i>

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.990
I'm coming to your apartment tomorrow.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.930
<i>Is showing him my life here 
at the apartments really okay?</i>

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.680
<i>If he...</i>

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.830
Hey.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.570
Hey.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.050
Can I leave my bike here?

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:41.850
Yeah.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.500
Come in.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.300
Help me with this.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.220
What is that?

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.640
These people have been helping you.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.810
I couldn't come empty-handed, right?

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.620
That's an exaggeration.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.160
Hase, before I introduce you to everyone,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.410
I have to tell you something.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.430
<b>Eighth Haunting 
Bookmaster</b>

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:42.880
Yushi-kun!

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.920
Akine-san!

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.810
Is that Hase-kun?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.980
Yes. Hase, this is Kuga Akine-san.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.290
Nice to meet you—

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:56.240
Hello. I am Hase Mizuki.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.940
Thank you for everything you do for Inaba.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.320
This is a token of my gratitude.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.250
These flowers are for me?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:04.510
Wow!

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.080
Yes. Also...

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.990
I can see people laughing at me 
for bringing a girl chocolates,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.710
but Inaba told me you enjoy eating.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.040
Here.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.710
So pretty! So cute! Thank you, Hase-kun!

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.040
Come on in. Everyone's waiting!

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.440
Of course.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.610
This way!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.130
Excuse me.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.740
Wait, Hase!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.920
Look, look! Hase-kun gave me these!

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.620
How pretty.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.370
You look like an old Japanese singer.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.590
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.490
So that's Hase-kun?

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.430
Y-Yes.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.800
I am Hase Mizuki.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.930
Thank you for all you do for Inaba.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.320
I hope you'll continue to be kind to him!

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.540
Oh?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.080
I see.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.710
<b><i>Hot Springs Manjuu</i></b>

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.710
So you brought something for us, too?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.960
Yes.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.030
If you'd be willing to accept it.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.610
Vintage wine!

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.380
I heard everyone likes alcohol...

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.040
Please have it with this.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.380
Classy.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.810
That ain't a proper present for a kid to give.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.690
I'm sorry. This is simply who I am.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.810
<i>They're actually getting along, aren't they?</i>

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.020
<i>However... I guess this 
is where it gets tough.</i>

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.550
Okay, Hase.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.900
Yeah.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.530
You may not believe me,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.450
but humans aren't the only inhabitants here.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.400
Yokai, ghosts, spirits...

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.380
I live with creatures known as those things.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.910
I've met a lot of people here.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.290
And I've learned a lot.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.590
And?

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.600
Aren't you letting me meet those 
who've done so much for you?

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.930
<i>If he won't accept them, then what will I do?</i>

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.450
Kuri!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.580
I can touch them... Wow.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.630
Ghosts are totally normal!

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.420
They really are amazing!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.050
Hase...

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.240
All kinds of yokai are here, huh?

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.080
Yeah.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.980
They've all been great to me.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.410
Ruriko-san?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.490
This is... Ruriko-san?

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.420
Y-Yeah.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:07.220
The Ruriko-san whose cooking 
you're always bragging about?

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.290
That's right.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:15.140
Ruriko-san! It's thanks to your 
meals that Inaba is healthy!

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.240
Thank you so much!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.550
This is for you.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.790
It's a rose hand cream I bought in Bali.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.010
Please accept it.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.130
Ruriko-san's blushing!

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.040
So classy.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.170
He's gonna get far in life.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.160
Ruriko-san made tea, 
so let's have these, too.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.240
<b><i>Famous Manjuu</i></b>

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.980
Why don't we have some of these?

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.660
How much did you bring?!

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.690
I'm glad I had enough presents...

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.650
You're amazing.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:50.720
Spending time and money to make 
the right connections is my policy.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.190
I heard about Akine-san, 
Ruriko-san, and the others, but...

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.560
Yay!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.640
S-Sorry!

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.370
Thanks so much.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.900
I'm glad the yokai like them, too.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.820
<i>Huh. Guess I shouldn't have worried.</i>

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.890
Is it good, chirp?

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.460
Let go, chirp!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.980
No, you let go, chirp!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.500
Chirpity-chirp!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.130
That's right, Hase-kun!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.780
You're staying for dinner, aren't you?

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.560
Ruriko-san wanted to know if 
you'd like anything in particular.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.010
Whatever Ruriko-san makes!

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.640
Why not just stay the night?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.850
Of course! That was the plan!

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.090
No one told me! Where will you sleep?

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:43.820
Your room, of course.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.670
My room has only one futon...

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:47.850
Then we can share.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.100
No! We aren't in elementary school!

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.150
I'm not sleeping next to you!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.480
But I am...

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.490
I am not!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.990
Isn't a sleep-over with a friend lots of fun?

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:01.090
Not with two guys.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.270
As thanks, Ruriko-san put 
extra effort into this.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.220
Thank you! I love it!

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.360
Pilchard fish balls and 
tomato soup... So good!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.520
I don't usually like pilchard, but this is great.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.930
Wow. It's like food you'd get at an inn.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.020
This sea bream tempura is amazing!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:21.990
It's fried without batter, isn't it?

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.660
The refreshing sweet vinegar pairs 
well with the rice! Seconds!

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.770
Akine-san, you've had four bowls!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.810
Isn't youth great?

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.700
This is better for grown-ups, though.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.810
Oh, Kuri-tan, what is it?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.500
You want this?

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.220
Kuri-tan, I don't know if you'll like it...

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.120
See?

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:56.720
<b>Men</b>

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.890
A real stone bath!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.930
Wow! It's so hot!

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.470
You're over-excited. 
It isn't that big a deal.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:07.350
Why not? Normally, you'd never get this.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.440
You have yummy food, 
and the bath is a hot spring.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.820
It's like a high-class inn!

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.340
You're right.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.030
I'm so jealous, you bastard!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:16.650
Wha?

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.620
Hey, what are you doing, you bastard?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.330
Now you've done it!

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:48.080
Whoa...

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.900
This is...

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.990
I guess they started throwing 
a party for you, Hase-kun.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.520
Without him actually here?

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.270
These people will use any excuse for a party.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.080
Are you going to the hospital?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.240
Yeah. Bye.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.360
Bye!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.520
It's so pretty.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.130
Yeah.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:35.230
<b><i>The Tanuki's Friends</i></b>

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.720
Want to read it together?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.560
Okay, sure.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.740
<b><i>The Tanuki's Friends</i></b>

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.130
Hey, Inaba...

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.610
Doing this, don't I look like a dad?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:08.230
<b><i>The Tanuki's Friends</i></b>

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.540
What are you talking about?

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.840
Kuri's so cute.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:05.820
He really is...

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.220
It doesn't matter that he's a ghost!

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.220
Yeah.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.220
W-W-W-Wait!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.310
Is that vintage wine?!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.350
You're back already?

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.960
Gimme a glass...

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.690
Sorry, just ran out!

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.020
It was good.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:27.360
Monsters!

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:28.910
Furuhonya-san...

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.770
He's amazing.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:33.290
He brought three bottles.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.730
Three bottles, and you 
already drank them all?

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.840
You yokai drunks! Drink-hogs!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.100
That isn't very nice.

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:43.660
And who's that?

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.330
I'm Hase.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.300
<i>This again?</i>

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:51.100
Sorry, sorry.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.890
You must be surprised to find your 
friend living in a place like this.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.360
He's also training to be a mage.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.270
But you know, being a mage 
isn't really a big deal.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:05.190
No, thank you for all you do for Inaba.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.690
I'm just a carrier...

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:10.110
Did you get something new?

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:10.960
Yeah.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.920
I found something interesting. 
I'll show you later.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.800
Thanks for the meal!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.130
Okay, now that my stomach's filled...

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:23.800
Back to drinking!

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.520
Wow.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.040
Every day is like this here.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.190
Seriously?

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:31.400
Seriously!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:37.520
Inaba, you've seen many 
things I never have, huh?

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:38.530
Yeah.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:42.670
But I still have no idea what's coming next!

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.320
What could that be?

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.330
An earthquake?

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:52.540
What?

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.160
The suitcase?

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.560
Oh, that's me, huh?

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.040
You brought something else weird?

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.260
Maybe...

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:05.460
Sorry. Guys, could you step back a little?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.730
H-H-Heads?!

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.930
Called it.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:21.710
They absorbed the place's spiritual 
energy and gained power.

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:24.200
Wh-Why are you analyzing this so calmly?

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.690
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:28.150
<i>Akine-san isn't here, and neither is Ryu-san!</i>

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:30.370
<i>Who else can fight those things?</i>

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.060
<i>Just me?</i>

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.280
<i>But...</i>

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.800
Hase! Kuri!

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.970
<i>I'm the only one.</i>

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.760
<i>I have to do it!</i>

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.420
Okay, okay. Don't worry.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:53.150
Furuhonya-san...

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:58.610
Leave it to me.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.360
There's a reason I can deal with these books.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:03.770
<i>Seven Sages.</i>

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.850
A book? A magical book?

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.300
Alatreon.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:25.330
It's gone?

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:29.640
Furuhonya-san, what are you?

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:33.670
A master of books from every 
historical period.

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:37.640
Everything from great literary 
works to ordinary paperbacks.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.820
But I specialize in the strange and unusual.

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:45.240
And people call me the "Bookmaster."

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.150
The Bookmaster?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.720
A guy who runs a bookstore?

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:49.880
<i>Welcome.</i>

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.050
No! Like "master of magical books"!

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.780
Magical books!

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:56.770
By the way, I'm not a magical girl!

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:56.770
<b>Self-Censorship</b>

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:58.460
No one asked.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.740
Do you have a magic book, too?

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:06.910
Yes, most mages have their own.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:12.440
Those who draw power from a book, 
like you or I, are called Bookmasters.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.800
We can make a contract with a book

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:19.350
and draw upon the power of 
what's on the other side.

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:20.950
The other side...

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:24.020
My book, <i>Seven Sages</i>,

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:26.940
contains the power of seven mages.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:30.930
And I can use that power however I like.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:34.670
Why didn't you say so earlier?

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.460
It's embarrassing!

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:37.480
And...

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:38.330
And?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.380
I'm on a whole different 
level than you, right?

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:43.380
Right.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.430
So this is an old book with 
a yokai sealed in it?

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:50.910
This place's spiritual energy 
gave it power, huh?

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:54.050
But I didn't expect the seal to break.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.900
This building never fails to disappoint.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.560
Come on...

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.000
Well, it happens.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.710
Make sure not to get devoured 
by any books, boy...

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.230
Jeez!

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.140
I really have only the one futon, okay?

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.290
No complaints.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.040
Hase?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.030
What's wrong?

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:26.370
Hey, you okay?

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.680
That scared me.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.520
Flying severed heads... What the hell?

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.270
And they attacked us?

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:38.010
Yeah, but it was fine, right?

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.740
This is all new to me!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.510
Yokai and ghosts...

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:46.980
I never thought I'd cross paths 
with occult stuff like that.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.610
And then, things like that show up.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.500
It's terrifying...

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:58.320
Hase, have you been scared the whole day?

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.520
Jeez!

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:05.470
Who the hell wouldn't be scared 
after seeing spirits and griffins?

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:08.090
I couldn't sleep a wink that night!

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:11.530
And now I'm in an apartment 
filled with yokai.

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.840
That could terrify even me!

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.090
<i>Yeah, that's normal.</i>

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.620
<i>At first, I was the same way.</i>

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.910
<i>Yokai and ghosts...</i>

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.670
<i>They aren't so easy to accept.</i>

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.730
Still, you know...

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.220
I was surprised to see all these new things.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.360
But this is a good place!

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:46.930
Thank you.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:50.180
Sure.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.290
Hey, let go of me already.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:57.770
Huh? Oh, sorry.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.750
Kuri! How long have you been there?!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.150
That's it, huh?

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.350
He wants to sleep next to you.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.870
Hey.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:23.230
Hmm?

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:26.790
Sleeping like this, we feel 
like a family, huh?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.830
Maybe.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.780
I'm the dad, and you're the mom.

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:32.710
Shut your mouth!

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:35.610
Crap, I woke up Kuri.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:37.620
What a bad mommy!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.230
Stop that!

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:40.950
Come on, don't cry...

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.970
Please summon Sirene, master.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.610
You're the one from before.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:50.270
Hello, again.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.360
Fool, who's Sirene?

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:56.450
A fairy who sings magical songs!

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.650
Songs.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.110
I get it!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.030
Sirene, sing a lullaby.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.820
Wow...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.220
Nice job.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.580
Yeah, I'm glad it worked.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.100
But of course...

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:28.200
Tonight, the waves we received 
from you were splendid.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.260
The waves?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.510
Indeed.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:36.170
Beautiful, shining waves, strong and supple!

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.810
Your growth makes us happy!

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:42.950
What's wrong?

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.380
Nothing.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.900
Let's go to sleep, too.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:04.400
<i>If I have grown, it's because...</i>

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.510
Thanks for everything.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.940
No, if anything...

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.570
Thanks for the presents, chirp.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.770
Next time, bring meat, chirp! Meat!

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.180
Black-haired wagyu, chirp!

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.530
Aren't macaroons yummy, chirp?

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.990
Thank you!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.930
We're the ones who should thank you.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:28.900
Everyone, I'll be—

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.240
I'll be back...

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.150
Yeah.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.870
<i>I'd been worried for so long.</i>

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.850
<i>No matter how comfy the apartment</i>

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.740
<i>or how everyone supported me,</i>

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.670
<i>I was so worried.</i>

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.170
<i>But Hase accepted it.</i>

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:52.510
<i>That's enough to keep me going.</i>

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.210
You're doing way better.

00:20:58.210 --> 00:20:59.940
You can tell, can't you?

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:00.710
Yeah!

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.600
Next time, I'll have to 
make it harder, right?

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:04.300
Right!

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:05.220
Huh?!

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.910
Since Hase-kun left, Kuri's seemed lonely.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.950
I guess he really liked him.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.100
Yeah.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.390
It's okay, Kuri.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.970
Daddy will be back soon.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:19.820
Daddy?

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:25.120
No, Hase... Hase said he was 
like a daddy on his day off!

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.960
Then, Yushi-kun, you're the mom, huh?

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:31.840
<i>Not you, too.</i>

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.680
What are you talking about?

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.150
Yushi-kun just said—

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:38.130
Stop! You don't really need to tell him!

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:12.960
We're finally in our second year.

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.630
What will school be like, start—

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:17.730
We're in the same class now, Inaba!

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:19.750
If something happens, come to me, okay?

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.040
I mean, I can help you. I know 
lots of people, and I'm popular!

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.280
And... And...

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.480
Things are going to get busy.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.880
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.180
New Term.

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.180
<b>Ninth Haunting 
New Term</b>

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:35.980
Hey, isn't there something weird about 
the new teacher, Miura-sensei?
